# Vercel builds and deploys the source it is given. Everything below stays on
# this machine: it holds real customer names, phone numbers, faces, sessions and
# credentials, none of which the running site needs in order to be built.
#
# Listed individually rather than as `.env.*` so `.env.example` — a template with
# placeholder values only — keeps travelling with the code.
.env
.env.local
.env.production
data/
uploads/
.vercel
.git
node_modules
*.log
